commit 9d48bd0ae82147d68c075e5ece4c3d946dc424a8
Author: fangyibo <fangyibo@xiaomi.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 20:10:16 2026 +0800

    chips/bes: fix JPEG M2M hardware decode

    Bring the V4L2 M2M JPEG decoder to a working state on the video PP:

    1. Call NextPicture before PictureConsumed, not the reverse.
    2. Keep the PP scaler disabled instead of running it at 1:1.
    3. Register the output buffer before querying buffer info.
    4. Register each buffer once, not on every frame.
    5. Decode into the CAPTURE buffer, not the compressed input one.
    6. Size sizeimage from the MCU padded height, not the visible one.
    7. Flush the destination before the DMA, not just invalidate after.
    8. Trace the opening frames only, not every frame.
    9. Make close idempotent against a second call.

    Previously only the first frame decoded, and once buffers were
    registered per frame the decode died on frame 34: the ctrlSW keeps
    them in a fixed array with no way to remove one.  Verified byte exact
    against two software decoders, and preview now runs unbounded.

    Change-Id: Ia9e595697fd349b93d00715be7de2ac279618570
    Signed-off-by: fangyibo <fangyibo@xiaomi.com>

